# One manifestation of the unified module-global-untagged-read defect
# (doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_run_file_pipeline_gaps_2026-07-30.md sections
# 9-10): a plain-literal module-level global reads wrong when accessed
# DIRECTLY (Y_direct), while a function call returning the same value
# (get_helper_y(), Y_via_fn) is correct -- because a function RETURN
# re-boxes the value and a direct global load does not. The cross-module
# `use` boundary is not the relevant axis (see section 9.4); compare
# module_global_direct_read_untagged.spl, which reproduces the identical
# defect same-file, with no import at all. Silent, no crash,
# SIMPLE_JIT_STRICT does not catch it.
#
# FIXED 2026-07-30 (doc section 11): unannotated module-level val/var
# (Node::Let) now infers a concrete type from a const-evaluable initializer
# instead of defaulting to ANY, so HELPER_Y correctly gets boxed before
# flowing into print(). known_good is now "both".
# Expected (both engines, correct): Y_direct=99 Y_via_fn=99
use helper_mod.{get_helper_y, HELPER_Y}

fn main():
    print("Y_direct={HELPER_Y} Y_via_fn={get_helper_y()}")
